  "entry": "10665-273155-por",
  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-001",
      "source": "sections/page-001.md",
      "source_hash": "08ae7bda6ca8f7e47d6a152e8525b55fbea302c7fe45c77e3645abb5acda5aa1",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The cover page of a 2018 WHO technical report in Portuguese giving a programmatic update on HIV diagnosis and antiretroviral use in HIV-exposed infants.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-002",
      "source": "sections/page-002.md",
      "source_hash": "442a32f19b55715990cc94afd40f984d9a1ca4e6bccb2b35b8069e8e77e5da9f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The copyright page, with the document number, Creative Commons licence terms, suggested citation and the WHO disclaimers.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-003",
      "source": "sections/page-003.md",
      "source_hash": "b975a1998e24621feeb6161fd6ee191920642c209a410c845b88a5d9c83abb93",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A summary explaining that new HIV infections in children continue and that innovations from WHO's 2016 consolidated guidelines, such as birth testing and point-of-care nucleic acid testing, have been adopted by few countries. It says the update draws on a 2017 Johannesburg workshop and a 2018 Geneva expert meeting, followed by a list of acronyms.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-004",
      "source": "sections/page-004.md",
      "source_hash": "26c4aa47c786cb3db5b45dcb29716d1e646e54993a1d6fc9070fb9e16e26e2bd",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reviews the state of paediatric HIV, noting large falls in new child infections under the Global Plan but 180 000 new infections in 2017 and a growing share of transmission during breastfeeding. It describes the challenges of retaining mothers in care and includes a chart of transmission rates by country.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-005",
      "source": "sections/page-005.md",
      "source_hash": "8971b6425b45ce874f467ff51f501ba86b195cb8983bac757015f1cbdcad71fd",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that only about half of children living with HIV were on treatment in 2017 and that untreated infant mortality is very high. It then sets out the rationale for the update, including more false-positive nucleic acid test results as transmission falls, delayed antibody development due to drug exposure and the lack of guidance on indeterminate results.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-006",
      "source": "sections/page-006.md",
      "source_hash": "04bda3b9ac2e82c29932dd246af22119de78434929fa7ff10d0a5c3219548102",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Presents evidence that using an indeterminate range for infant nucleic acid tests could prevent many false-positive diagnoses, and explains the choice of a cycle-threshold cut-off. It mentions South Africa's operating procedure and a new WHO procedure, and defines terms such as indeterminate and discordant results.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-007",
      "source": "sections/page-007.md",
      "source_hash": "b725bb2430d2fb2ed926511139b294573c2ca6361443ea9868b2f77cecb7d2b1",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that infants with repeated indeterminate results should be followed up, and that point-of-care early infant diagnosis can now be used to confirm positive results. It then discusses managing discordant results and deciding whether to stop treatment, and lists key recommendations such as confirming all positive results with a new sample.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-008",
      "source": "sections/page-008.md",
      "source_hash": "fde520eb051c95df90b8e0788d2c664470ef518353f893d4fbb9a04f7f989da8",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes implementation of point-of-care early infant diagnosis, citing studies in Malawi and Mozambique showing faster results and treatment start. It lists lessons from pilots on site selection, maintenance and integration, and urges regulators to approve prequalified products quickly.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-009",
      "source": "sections/page-009.md",
      "source_hash": "12e4ba80b07d62bfc6104ff2ecb3862b5b0a8fb3c7564657d18d292c90ef3ad0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports experience with HIV testing at birth, which mothers accept but which strains staff and systems. A box describes the programmes in South Africa and Kenya and their challenges, and the page ends with key considerations, such as linkage to treatment and strong leadership.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-010",
      "source": "sections/page-010.md",
      "source_hash": "b8fc4d944e922eb6135e64f106cbff87aed98134db08b31a2eb178e7e80e35c3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A page with no extracted text.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-011",
      "source": "sections/page-011.md",
      "source_hash": "e3e032b322851acc95c164cd79bc902ace5fcbe6687a94a0193df07429070a66",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Discusses how drug exposure and late maternal infection have made rapid antibody tests less reliable for determining infant HIV status at 9 months. It recommends simplifying the testing algorithm, including using nucleic acid testing at 9 months and testing mothers to establish exposure.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-012",
      "source": "sections/page-012.md",
      "source_hash": "81c6f4be10d492d732ad98c94f7840cf378ecb7d7d0adfa253ec7ff195d1ef56",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Covers challenges in giving enhanced postnatal prophylaxis to high-risk infants, explaining WHO's dual zidovudine and nevirapine regimen and how high risk is defined. It describes the varied approaches countries have taken and the need to reassess mothers and infants regularly.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-013",
      "source": "sections/page-013.md",
      "source_hash": "0d19c357c5bb8927e6ce971038d50fe9525fb6f38ea1995b6d3e8d1d9d6123c9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Discusses whether high-risk infants might receive a three-drug presumptive treatment regimen and the need to collect a test sample first. It then describes the limited and hard-to-administer treatment options for newborns and young infants and the potential of fixed-dose combinations.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-014",
      "source": "sections/page-014.md",
      "source_hash": "e296c389e8af5908c7f1fe068be17c3fbb5f8de08d0cb17140aeff054ce3004f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes integrating care for HIV-exposed infants into maternal, newborn and child health services, linked information systems and community-based services, including networks of women living with HIV.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-273155-por/blocks/prose-page-015",
      "source": "sections/page-015.md",
      "source_hash": "c0f1f12c694d2408c4e430fe8ad08034c19b3a0c4cf4992b2965009f7a1bac90",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists priority research questions on paediatric diagnosis, prophylaxis and treatment, such as the value of birth testing and new antiretroviral formulations. It closes by noting that strategies must be adapted to changing epidemics and policies and supported by more programme experience.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
