      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Annex 5 of the Portuguese edition of the WHO update on HIV diagnosis and ARV use in exposed infants, a table comparing syrup, tablet and fixed-dose combination options for giving AZT and nevirapine prophylaxis to infants over 0–12 weeks. It lists doses with the pros and cons of each option and notes that AZT has no separate prophylactic dose, so treatment doses apply.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
